  "question": {
    "text": "Determine the lengths of an iron rod and a copper ruler at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> if the difference in their lengths at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is the same and is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The coefficient of linear expansion of iron = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and that of copper = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.",
